#: ../../source/export.rst:4 71bd5cf6695d48158587991e59ab69c7
msgid ""
"Brief overview: the library :code:`stereo_vision` turns a calibrated "
"stereo pair into a disparity map, a depth map and a point cloud. The "
"chain is: epipolar rectification, SGBM matching, disparity to depth, "
"depth to point cloud."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/export.rst:9 e49a8a1d97d74c93b323f324aded0c91
msgid "_`Theories or introduction`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/export.rst:11 113138d78c3c4937bc7198efe4501204
msgid ""
"A rectified stereo pair observes one scene point from two positions. Once"
" the epipolar lines are horizontal, the horizontal coordinate difference "
"of the match is the disparity :math:`d`, and depth follows from the "
"rectified geometry:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/export.rst:15 508a78b1c5594cb0881c0028809be642
msgid ""
"Z = \\frac{f_x \\, |T_x|}{d - d_{offs}}, \\qquad d_{offs} = c_{x1} - "
"c_{x2}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/export.rst:20 b87da8e616af42ce9b74995db5bb0632
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
":math:`f_x` is the rectified focal length, :math:`T_x` the baseline "
"component along the camera x axis, and :math:`c_{x1}, c_{x2}` the "
"horizontal principal points of the two rectified views. The data term is "
"the matching cost of the SGBM energy, the smoothness term is the penalty "
"paid when neighbouring pixels take different labels:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/export.rst:25 3b78bf547bbe411ca1f0b1f63c95f4a7
msgid ""
"E(D) = \\sum_p C(p, D_p) + \\sum_{q \\in \\mathcal{N}_p} P_1 \\, "
"\\delta(\\lvert D_p - D_q \\rvert = 1)\n"
"     + \\sum_{q \\in \\mathcal{N}_p} P_2 \\, \\delta(\\lvert D_p - D_q "
"\\rvert > 1)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/export.rst:30 51ae8a0ef11c42d28a5aa6289510814f
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The energy is minimised along several scanline directions and the per-"
"pixel minimum is kept, which is what lets textureless regions take a "
"plausible label instead of following noise. :math:`P_1` and :math:`P_2` "
"are derived from the block size: :math:`P_1 = p_1^{factor} b^2`, "
":math:`P_2 = p_2^{factor} b^2`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/export.rst:35 e61718f5ac634ec789c6953aca056247
msgid ""
"Three details make the difference between a usable result and a "
"plausible-looking one:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/export.rst:37 80d85268171f4b5d93ecc7e7c4aad19f
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
":math:`d_{offs}` is generally not zero. Dropping it shifts the whole "
"cloud sideways by :math:`d_{offs} Z / f_x`, while the depth values "
"themselves stay correct."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/export.rst:39 91cf28f30dbe484dbb62742673bf9af0
msgid ""
"Cropping to the common valid region translates the origin, so ``Q``'s "
"fourth column and the principal points of ``P1``/``P2`` must move with "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/export.rst:41 1a83b370590341b3b92729f4e9006560
msgid ""
"Remapping a white image through the same maps marks the pixels that "
"really carry data. Without that mask, the matcher reads the black border "
"as scene content and invents disparity there."
msgstr ""

